      "content": "Here's a revised speech that incorporates the requested elements:\n\n\"My fellow citizens, as we gather here today, it is essential to acknowledge the profound differences that separate our citizens into two distinct classes. The worker, with their sturdy build and robust physiology, is a testament to the unyielding power of natural selection. Their broad shoulders, capable hands, and sturdy legs are a direct result of millions of years of adaptation to a life of toil and labor. In contrast, our own refined features – our high cheekbones, slender builds, and agile minds – are the hallmarks of a civilization that has transcended the mundane drudgery of manual labor. The worker's temperament, too, is a reflection of their biology: their impulsive nature, their tendency towards aggression in the face of frustration, and their limited capacity for abstract thought all serve as a reminder that they are, by their very nature, ill-suited to the complexities of governance. The pseudo-scientific findings of our own research have amply demonstrated the correlation between cranial structure, cognitive ability, and social status – and it is clear that our own superior cranium, capable of housing the most advanced and sophisticated cognitive machinery, is the key to unlocking true greatness. To",
